From fe876184da748712760cf50106abdb13c3c07359 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VortaForge Archival <archival@vortaforge.local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:18:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(blocklist): organisation-wide datapack blocklist, mirror
 sync and profile scan

One squashed change set for `vortaforge/.github`, applied after the core patch.

  * `blocklist/blocklist.json` - the org-wide mirror of core's list, generated
    by the sync script and never hand-edited. Verified datapack tooling authors
    are blocked by login and numeric id; the maintainers are exempt through
    `managed.accounts` in core.
  * `generated/blocklist.json` - the same data for tooling that should not read
    the editable path.
  * `scripts/blocklist_sync.py` - `--check` fails on drift, `--write` updates
    the mirror, `--scan-profiles` reads PUBLIC profile fields only
    (`bio`, `company`, `name`, `blog`) for accounts that already interacted
    with the organisation. A hit opens an issue; it never blocks by itself.
  * `.github/workflows/datapack-blocklist-sync.yml` - daily sync plus profile
    scan, action pins by commit SHA, read-only except for the one commit step.

No account is ever blocked automatically, and no private data is read.
